      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><em>Waluipedia cast sheet — Director Mario.</em> Built by <code>tools/build-character-sheets.py</code>, hand-authored from the article. no XP ledger entry; archetype default → a level 3 Bard player-character sheet (a player may take this seat; the authored CR 3 stands in where the ledger is silent). Numbers are a GM-ready reading of the record, not a filed stat line; the article stays the authority. Archive date 1040 BF.</p><p><strong>The Man Wario Bows To</strong> — The Nintendo Mania studio — management</p><p>Status: Active — knocked Wario unconscious for ruining his show and walked out with a folder and a small wired remote</p><p>The figure who stepped out from behind the entire two-filing production: tall, director's cap, script under one arm, cigar, and no warmth anywhere. Wario — the showman, the Apparition, the boss of everyone visible — went pale and bowed and called him Boss, and was put through a wall for exceeding his brief.</p><h3>Evidence</h3><ul><li><strong>Backhand</strong> — “Active — knocked Wario unconscious for ruining his show and walked out with a folder and a small wired remote”</li><li><strong>CUT</strong> — “The Director's dossier fits on a cue sheet: he knew the show had gone over better than Wario thought, he knew the results, and he snapped his own cigar in half saying the quiet part out loud.”</li><li><strong>The Remote</strong> — “Active — knocked Wario unconscious for ruining his show and walked out with a folder and a small wired remote”</li><li><strong>The Man Wario Bows To</strong> — “The Man Wario Bows To”</li></ul><p>Article: <code>#/article/director_mario</code> (characters). Site sheet: <code>#/sheets/director_mario</code>.</p>",
        "public": ""
      }
